cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ccc-nulls, please cite it as below, and cite LIANA+ (Dimitrov et al. 2024), which it extends."
title: "ccc-nulls: a composite null for ligand-receptor specificity inside LIANA+'s consensus"
abstract: >-
  Permutation-based cell-cell communication tools (CellPhoneDB, CellChat, and LIANA+'s consensus built on them)
  call an interaction when either side is cell-type specific. ccc-nulls replaces their p-value with a composite
  null (intersection-union test) under which both the ligand side and the receptor side must be specific,
  computed from LIANA+'s own permutations, and benchmarks it on calibration, power and biological ground truth.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "ccc-nulls contributors"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-11-04"
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/kshitij-bhardwaj/ccc-nulls"
keywords:
  - single-cell
  - cell-cell communication
  - ligand-receptor
  - permutation test
  - intersection-union test
  - LIANA
references:
  - type: article
    title: "LIANA+ provides an all-in-one framework for cell-cell communication inference"
    authors:
      - family-names: Dimitrov
        given-names: Daniel
    journal: "Nature Cell Biology"
    volume: 26
    start: 1613
    end: 1622
    year: 2024
